# Execute requests individually, in order, using an HTTP client with a Cookie jar.
# Use a dedicated test account. Do not commit real credentials or tokens here.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth
@email = 20260001@bjtu.edu.cn
@password = Foodtime2026!
@verificationCode = replace_with_6_digits_from_email
@csrfToken = replace_with_data_token_from_csrf_response

### 1. Get an anonymous CSRF token. Preserve the Set-Cookie response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/csrf
Accept: application/json

### 2. Set csrfToken above to response data.token, then send the email code.
POST {{baseUrl}}/register/email-code
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### 3. Set verificationCode above to the emailed six-digit string (15-minute expiry).
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "verificationCode": "{{verificationCode}}"
}

### 4. Get the current CSRF token before login; keep the same Cookie jar.
GET {{baseUrl}}/csrf
Accept: application/json

### 5. Update csrfToken from step 4. Login replaces the anonymous session Cookie.
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "account": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 6. Get a NEW CSRF token after login; the previous token is invalidated.
GET {{baseUrl}}/csrf
Accept: application/json

### 7. Verify the current user using the login session Cookie.
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Accept: application/json

### 8. Update csrfToken from step 6. Logout deletes the current session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### 9. The previous login session must no longer authenticate: expect 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Accept: application/json
